Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: clear BMCR power-down before autoneg

Linux's genphy_suspend leaves the ADIN1300 PHY in software power-down
across a warm reboot, and nothing else in U-Boot clears the bit. Left
set, autonegotiation never completes and dhcp times out waiting on
the link. Clear the power-down bit before running the existing
autoneg configuration so a warm reboot after Linux brings the link up
the same way a cold power-on does.

Signed-off-by: Larry Ruckman <ruckman@slac.stanford.edu>
Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/drivers/net/phy/adin.c	2026-09-26 19:45:32.895038546 -0700
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/adin.c	2026-09-26 19:45:50.877196567 -0700
@@ -260,6 +260,26 @@
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Linux's genphy_suspend leaves the PHY in software power-down
+	 * across a warm reboot, and nothing else in U-Boot clears the bit.
+	 * If left set, autonegotiation never completes and dhcp times out
+	 * waiting on the link, so clear it here and kick off a fresh
+	 * autoneg on the powered PHY.
+	 */
+	ret = phy_read(phydev, MDIO_DEVAD_NONE, MII_BMCR);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+
+	if (ret & BMCR_PDOWN) {
+		printf("%s: clearing BMCR power-down before autoneg\n",
+		       phydev->drv->name);
+		ret = phy_modify(phydev, MDIO_DEVAD_NONE, MII_BMCR,
+				  BMCR_PDOWN, BMCR_ANRESTART);
+		if (ret < 0)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	return genphy_config(phydev);
 }
 
